  <h2 id="layers">Three layers</h2>
  <p>The crate has three layers, and each layer uses only the layers below it. A role never uses a
  deployment, and a deployment never uses another deployment. CI checks this with
  <code>scripts/check-core-layers.sh</code>.</p>
  <div class="arch" role="img" aria-label="Three layers. Deployments on top: ColocatedNode, ProxyLeader, ReplicaNode, Matchmaker. Roles in the middle: proposer, acceptor, replica, quorum reads, decree, batcher. Foundations at the bottom: types, journal, contract.">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="box lead">deployments <small>ColocatedNode · ProxyLeader · ReplicaNode · Matchmaker</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="arrow">▼ <small>wire</small></div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="box">roles <small>proposer · acceptor · replica · quorum_read · decree · batcher</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="arrow">▼ <small>use</small></div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="box side">foundations <small>types · journal · contract · membership</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>A role knows only what the caller gives it. The proposer builds no message, the acceptor
  never reads the chosen prefix, and the replica never sees a ballot tally. Each quorum question
  goes through <code>membership</code> (<code>has_phase1_quorum</code>,
  <code>has_phase2_quorum</code>), so a new quorum system is a new <code>QuorumSystem</code>
  variant and no tally changes.</p>

  <h2 id="journal">The log is a journal</h2>
  <p>The log of <code>ColocatedNode</code> carries a journal: a <code>Write</code> appends records at
  a position, <code>SetLeader</code> names the client that may write, and <code>Truncate</code> drops
  a prefix. The core judges no command at <code>propose</code>. Each node judges a command when its
  slot is applied, in slot order, so each node gives the same <code>Outcome</code>. A write on a
  journal with no writer is chosen by Paxos and refused by the journal.</p>

